   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "In the kitchen and at the table",
     "texto": [
      "In the kitchen: **freír** (in oil), **hervir** (in water), **asar** (in the oven), **batir** eggs, **pelar** potatoes, **aliñar** a salad.\n\nTo **poner la mesa**: the **mantel**, the **servilletas**, the plates, the glasses and the **cubiertos**.\n\nTo tell about an accident without blaming anyone: **se me ha quemado** la cena, **se me ha caído** un plato. The thing is the subject and the person goes in **me / te / le / nos / os / les**.\n\nMeat can be **poco hecha**, **en su punto** or **muy hecha**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "What happens by accident",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something happens by accident, we use **se** + **me / te / le / nos / os / les** + verb:\n\n- **Se me ha quemado** la cena.\n- **Se me ha caído** un plato.\n- **Se me han olvidado** las servilletas.\n\nThe thing that burns, falls or is forgotten is the **subject**: the verb agrees with it (**ha quemado**, **han olvidado**).\n\nThe pronoun **me** says who suffers the accident. With **haber**, the participle does not change: se me han olvidado."
     ],
